WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.992
[MUSIC]

00:00:00.992 --> 00:00:03.420
Artificial Intelligence is everywhere.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.650
Every company is taking advantage of it,
or needs to take advantage of it.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:12.144
We at Stanford are thinking about
that across the university,

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:18.008
both the business point of view, but
also, actually the societal point of view.

00:00:18.008 --> 00:00:20.473
[MUSIC]

00:00:20.473 --> 00:00:23.310
&gt;&gt; To a lot of people, AI is just magic.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.461
Through this program,

00:00:24.461 --> 00:00:28.495
they can have a little bit of a better
understanding of what's actually entailed.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:32.189
&gt;&gt; Honestly,
it was fear that drove me here [LAUGH].

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:37.090
I mean, everywhere you just keep on
hearing about AI, and what are you doing.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.122
I'm a non technical person,

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:42.708
I want to makes sure that
I'm on the forefront to Fit.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.860
&gt;&gt; Data per se is very valuable.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:48.952
However, if you don't apply it and
you don't put it in the right algorithms,

00:00:48.952 --> 00:00:50.881
you also not get much value out of it.

00:00:50.881 --> 00:00:55.643
&gt;&gt; Each day starts with an overview
provided by a world class faculty member,

00:00:55.643 --> 00:00:57.769
who's an expert in their field.

00:00:57.769 --> 00:01:03.620
No equations, nothing complicated
going on, just high level insights.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.561
And then, later on,
we take a either a deeper dive, or

00:01:07.561 --> 00:01:12.877
we have someone from industry talk
about some of the issues in translating

00:01:12.877 --> 00:01:18.987
some of the ongoing research in artificial
intelligence, and to business impact.

00:01:18.987 --> 00:01:20.252
&gt;&gt; To better understand,

00:01:20.252 --> 00:01:23.740
what's the [INAUDIBLE] regulatory
ethical framework around it.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.330
Yeah, I thought, on the other hand, what

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:30.990
can we do in order to improve customer
experience or create additional revenues.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:35.580
So combining those two perspectives,
I think it's a great value of the program.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:40.140
&gt;&gt; What's really great about this program
is we're drawing from all of campus.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.280
We have some great people coming
in from the engineering school,

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.280
the business school.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.082
And we've also brought in someone from the
medical school to bring that perspective,

00:01:48.082 --> 00:01:49.237
as well as the law school.

00:01:49.237 --> 00:01:50.435
[MUSIC]

00:01:50.435 --> 00:01:54.270
If you're going to learn about AI,
you want to do it here in Silicon Valley.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.210
This is where everything is happening.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:01.470
&gt;&gt; We're within a few miles of many of
the companies that are implementing AI,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.350
as part of their core business strategy.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:09.885
&gt;&gt; Whether I'm an engineer, whether I'm
in finance, whether I'm in public sector,

00:02:09.885 --> 00:02:10.897
doesn't matter.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.660
Things are changing fast.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.740
What do we need to do?

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:17.099
&gt;&gt; There's just really
no place like Stanford,

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:20.610
in terms of bringing all of this
expertise together in one place.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:24.700
&gt;&gt; I saw this program, and
it's a brilliant way to get introduced.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.060
And there's that personal touch.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.780
And there's this one week
of intensive learning.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:32.900
So I mean, this environment,
you can't beat it.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.339
[MUSIC]

